==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*bogъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|phon=бох}}
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|Ru-бог.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

In the nominative singular, the word is usually pronounced {{IPAchar|/box/}} (as if spelled {{lang|ru|бох}}) due to Church Slavonic influence. The regular pronunciation {{IPAchar|/bok/}} is used only rarely. In all other case forms, the regular {{IPAchar|/ɡ/}} is more common, but older pronunciations used {{IPAchar|/ɣ/}}.

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|e|nom_sg=бог//box|voc=бо́же|a=an|f=боги́ня}}

# [[God]]
# [[god]], [[idol]]
#: {{ru-ux|бог [[он|его́]] [[знать|зна́ет]]!|God only knows!; goodness knows!|inline=y|sub=бог/бох}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[бо́же]] [[мой]]!|oh God!; good gracious!|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|бог [[с]] [[он|ним]]!|Forget him!|inline=y|sub=бог/бох}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[давать|дай]] бог!|God willing!; let’s hope so!|inline=y|sub=бог/бох}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[ей-бо́гу]]!|really!; really and truly!|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[ра́ди]] бо́га!|for God’s sake!|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[сохранять|сохрани́]] [[бо́же]]!|God forbid!|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[сла́ва бо́гу]]!|thank God!|inline=y}}

====Usage notes====
* Usually not capitalized in Russian in the sense of [[idol]], or when referring to a single god with a polytheistic pantheon. Capitalized in monotheistic sense, such as in Islamic or Christian discourse (see {{m|ru|Бог|tr=Box}}).

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|e|nom_sg=бог//box|voc=бо́же|a=an}}

====Related terms====
